+      "sourceText": "Timing changes which part of the structure becomes most prominent, but no specific Luck Pillars or annual influences have been supplied, so no age, year, or event can be assigned. At the level of general principle only, periods that emphasize Earth and Metal may bring greater attention to carrying capacity, integration, method, peer support, and the construction of boundaries. Whether that is favorable in a particular period still depends on the complete configuration and cannot be decided mechanically from one element. Stronger Water and Wood themes may emphasize communication, project flow, result demands, and resource conversion. This can enlarge visible production, while also increasing leakage on the weaker side of the Day Master. Fire must be read on separate levels: as seasonal regulation it may provide warmth and activation, while in practical operation it may appear as rules, deadlines, pressure, or momentum. Its effect depends on whether the Earth and Metal foundation can carry it. Since the natal Three Harmony configuration is not a complete Water transformation, timing does not erase the other hidden stems or their original structural meanings.",
