+    &quot;end&quot;: 843,
+    &quot;sourceText&quot;: &quot;In relationships and intimacy, Wealth cannot be mechanically equated with a particular spouse, nor can its placement establish facts about marriage. A more reliable interpretation concerns how expression and personal choice are connected with practical responsibility. The existing output-to-wealth pathway tends to validate a bond through problem-solving, workable arrangements, and the investment of time or resources, rather than leaving the relationship entirely at the level of feeling or intention. Visible Indirect Wealth supports responsiveness to changing circumstances, while concealed Direct Wealth adds an underlying concern with continuity, detail, and defined obligation. Relational ease therefore depends not only on whether care is present, but on whether what is expressed can become an arrangement that both people can carry.&quot;,
